fter I manually commented out the content from https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108350, the issue disappeared. Thanks!\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3124452870/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3124513643","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109024#issuecomment-3124513643","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109024","id":3124513643,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc66PEtr","user":{"login":"scgm0","id":52148221,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMTQ4MjIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52148221?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0","html_url":"https://github.com/scgm0","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-27T16:06:20Z","updated_at":"2025-07-27T16:06:20Z","body":"@DanielSnd Could you take a look at this issue?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3124513643/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3124699410","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109024#issuecomment-3124699410","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109024","id":3124699410,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc66PyES","user":{"login":"DanielSnd","id":9072324,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNzIzMjQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9072324?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielSnd","html_url":"https://github.com/DanielSnd","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielSnd/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielSnd/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielSnd/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielSnd/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielSnd/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielSnd/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielSnd/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielSnd/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielSnd/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-27T20:09:00Z","updated_at":"2025-07-27T20:09:00Z","body":"> After I manually commented out the content from [#108350](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108350), the issue disappeared. Thanks!\n\nInteresting, I'm not sure why those defines are causing the problem, can you try this instead of commenting those out and see if it also resolves the problem?\n\n```cpp\n#if defined(SDL_PLATFORM_PRIVATE) && defined(__linux__)\n#define HAVE_INOTIFY 1\n#define HAVE_INOTIFY_INIT1 1\n#define HAVE_GETENV 1\n#define HAVE_SETENV 1\n#define HAVE_UNSETENV 1\n#endif\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3124699410/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3124704421","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109024#issuecomment-3124704421","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109024","id":3124704421,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc66PzSl","user":{"login":"scgm0","id":52148221,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMTQ4MjIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52148221?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0","html_url":"https://github.com/scgm0","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-27T20:19:31Z","updated_at":"2025-07-27T20:19:31Z","body":"> Interesting, I'm not sure why those defines are causing the problem, can you try this instead of commenting those out and see if it also resolves the problem?\n> \n> #if defined(SDL_PLATFORM_PRIVATE) && defined(__linux__)\n> #define HAVE_INOTIFY 1\n> #define HAVE_INOTIFY_INIT1 1\n> #define HAVE_GETENV 1\n> #define HAVE_SETENV 1\n> #define HAVE_UNSETENV 1\n> #endif\n\nno\n\n<img width=\"1383\" height=\"1026\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e4b082bd-4a3c-45ee-9914-516e10ea5b9b\" />\n\n<img width=\"1282\" height=\"806\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8a14575a-566b-4733-930a-06401f0e7f9a\" />","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3124704421/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3124706929","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109024#issuecomment-3124706929","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109024","id":3124706929,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc66Pz5x","user":{"login":"scgm0","id":52148221,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMTQ4MjIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52148221?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0","html_url":"https://github.com/scgm0","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-27T20:24:53Z","updated_at":"2025-07-27T20:35:13Z","body":"<img width=\"1383\" height=\"1026\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7acd46cf-aa40-470a-8bdc-f35dbb232d70\" />\n\n<img width=\"1282\" height=\"806\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/08caa2d4-8131-4468-83a9-a6aeead79e81\" />\n\n~~It appears that the definition of `HAVE_UNSETENV` is causing the bug. What is its purpose?~~\nOh, no matter which one of `HAVE_GETENV`, `HAVE_SETENV`, or `HAVE_UNSETENV` is commented out, the same compilation result will be produced, and the issue can be resolved.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3124706929/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3127387613","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109024#issuecomment-3127387613","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109024","id":3127387613,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc66aCXd","user":{"login":"DanielSnd","id":9072324,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNzIzMjQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9072324?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielSnd","html_url":"https://github.com/DanielSnd","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielSnd/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielSnd/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielSnd/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielSnd/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielSnd/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielSnd/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielSnd/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielSnd/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielSnd/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-28T14:02:42Z","updated_at":"2025-07-28T14:02:42Z","body":"> ~It appears that the definition of `HAVE_UNSETENV` is causing the bug. What is its purpose?\n\nThe purpose is so SDL can have access to the environment variables in linux. The problem that started this is that when we moved Input to be handled by the SDL libraries the Steamdeck Controllers stopped working with godot. I tracked down the problem to it not picking up the Steamdeck's environment variables that allowed it to inject the needed information into SDL about its virtual controllers. Setting those defines allowed SDL to have access to the environment variables and solved the problem. They're being used here to define `HAVE_LIBC_ENVIRONMENT` if all of them are defined (or \"HAVE_PUTENV\" is defined alongside HAVE_GETENV). I wonder if the problem you're having is with `HAVE_LIBC_ENVIRONMENT`, because by commenting any of them out, `HAVE_LIBC_ENVIRONMENT` isn't defined there.\n\n```cpp\n#elif defined(HAVE_GETENV) && \\\n      (defined(HAVE_SETENV) || defined(HAVE_PUTENV)) && \\\n      (defined(HAVE_UNSETENV) || defined(HAVE_PUTENV))\n#define HAVE_LIBC_ENVIRONMENT\n```\nIn [/thirdparty/sdl/stdlib/SDL_getenv.c](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/8b2739ee55f8bebe7c4a20c55841851c4f411efe/thirdparty/sdl/stdlib/SDL_getenv.c#L35C9-L37C2)\n\nHAVE_UNSETENV is used down lower:\n\n```cpp\n#ifdef HAVE_LIBC_ENVIRONMENT\n#if defined(HAVE_UNSETENV)\nint SDL_unsetenv_unsafe(const char *name)\n{\n    // Input validation\n    if (!name || *name == '\\0' || SDL_strchr(name, '=') != NULL) {\n        return -1;\n    }\n\n    SDL_UnsetEnvironmentVariable(SDL_GetEnvironment(), name);\n\n    return unsetenv(name);\n}\n```\nIn [the same file](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/8b2739ee55f8bebe7c4a20c55841851c4f411efe/thirdparty/sdl/stdlib/SDL_getenv.c#L450)\n\nCan you try this? I think on our input's case we only need it to get the variables, not set it, so it shouldn't matter if it's using HAVE_PUTENV instead.\n```cpp\n#ifdef __linux__\n#define HAVE_INOTIFY 1\n#define HAVE_INOTIFY_INIT1 1\n#define HAVE_GETENV 1\n#define HAVE_PUTENV 1\n#endif\n```\n\nI don't know enough about SDL, or mono/C# so I'm not sure what could be happening. Maybe we can ping someone that knows more about the mono side of things? @Nintorch is the person that implemented the SDL Input so pinging them in case they can help.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3127387613/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3127436138","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109024#issuecomment-3127436138","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109024","id":3127436138,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc66aONq","user":{"login":"DanielSnd","id":9072324,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNzIzMjQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9072324?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielSnd","html_url":"https://github.com/DanielSnd","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielSnd/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielSnd/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielSnd/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielSnd/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielSnd/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielSnd/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielSnd/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielSnd/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielSnd/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-28T14:14:03Z","updated_at":"2025-07-28T14:14:11Z","body":"I guess one possible solution would be this, but then we have a new problem of Steamdeck controllers not working with Godot C# games:\n\n```cpp\n#ifndef MODULE_MONO_ENABLED\n#ifdef __linux__\n#define HAVE_INOTIFY 1\n#define HAVE_INOTIFY_INIT1 1\n#define HAVE_GETENV 1\n#define HAVE_SETENV 1\n#define HAVE_UNSETENV 1\n#endif\n#endif\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3127436138/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3128067822","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109024#issuecomment-3128067822","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109024","id":3128067822,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc66cobu","user":{"login":"Nintorch","id":92302738,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYBtkg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92302738?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch","html_url":"https://github.com/Nintorch","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-28T16:34:24Z","updated_at":"2025-07-28T16:34:24Z","body":"This is kind of a bizarre case, I've checked the source code of SDL to see if it unsets other environment variables just in case and I didn't find anything, the Godot's source code for get_environment() method (specifically, OS_Unix::get_environment) doesn't look weird either, so I'm really not sure why this is happening, sorry :(","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3128067822/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3128322062","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109024#issuecomment-3128322062","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109024","id":3128322062,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc66dmgO","user":{"login":"scgm0","id":52148221,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMTQ4MjIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52148221?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0","html_url":"https://github.com/scgm0","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-28T17:42:24Z","updated_at":"2025-07-28T17:42:24Z","body":"> Can you try this? I think on our input's case we only need it to get the variables, not set it, so it shouldn't matter if it's using HAVE_PUTENV instead.\n> \n> #ifdef __linux__\n> #define HAVE_INOTIFY 1\n> #define HAVE_INOTIFY_INIT1 1\n> #define HAVE_GETENV 1\n> #define HAVE_PUTENV 1\n> #endif\n\nThere are still issues with